{
  "dom_id": "step-q84037",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "The number of heads facing upward after tossing $3$ fair coins follows the probability mass function $f(x)$ shown in the table below. What is the expected value of the number of heads facing upward after tossing the $3$ coins?\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |",
  "worked_solution": "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{1}{8})+1(\\frac{3}{8})+2(\\frac{3}{8})+3(\\frac{1}{8}) \\\\  & =0+\\frac{3}{8}+\\frac{6}{8}+\\frac{3}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{0+3+6+3}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
